- **category**: "object" only for a movable thing someone could leave or pick up (a book, AirPods, a mug, paper). Use "person" for a body part or clothing, "lighting" for light, shadow or reflection, "screen" for a display, "furniture" for furniture or a door, "other" for anything else.
- **label**: a short name a person would use ("red book", "AirPods case", "sheet of paper"). Name a specific thing only if it is clearly that; otherwise describe what you see ("thin white sheet", "small dark object").
- **place**: where it is, relative to furniture ("on the desk, left of the laptop", "floor by the door").
